 structure. The building was designed by the British Royal Engineers Corps combining international architectural styles and is a testimony to past influences from Roman, Dutch and English styles on Kerala. The old Legislature Assembly Hall inside t","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Thiruvananthapuram","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3d/Secretariat_Kerala_%28old_building%29.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3d/Secretariat_Kerala_%28old_building%29.jpg","w":1200,"h":887,"author":"Kris Sreekandath","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Secretariat_Kerala_(old_building).jpg"}}],"sources":["Wikidata (CC0)","Wikimedia Commons (counts; photos credited per file)","Wikipedia (pageviews; summaries CC BY-SA 4.0)","Wikivoyage (listings: hours, prices, descriptions; CC BY-SA 4.0)","OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL): opening hours, fees, websites"]}